# AtaProjectCommon

Applies to SharedFrame, AlphaTerminal, Varlik360 and CeyizDefterim. Generator's own source is not produced by this rule. The host is the open project root that contains `.generator/manifest.json`.

- Rules are shared: every `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` in these hosts comes from Generator `src/generator-assets/cursor-rules/`. Only the "Bu projeye özel" section at the bottom of each file is edited in the host; a shared rule is changed in the Generator file and spread with `node /Users/atakanatabey/Projects/AtaAllWorkspace/Generator/scripts/rules-sync.mjs --apply`. A host that does not follow a rule yet says so in that section.
- Data layer: admin uses admin-base + TanStack Query for everything except auth; web and mobile use service + thunk + slice (`responseThunk` + `unwrap`). try/catch is banned in pages and components and allowed in thunks.
- One response shape everywhere: `{ isSuccess, data, uiMessage, errorData, traceId }`, lists as `PaginatedList` inside `data`. No envelope layer, `meta`, `PageMeta`, or client-side converter between the server and `LocalResponse`.

- Precedence for file names and locations: if Generator has an output for it (admin skeleton `src/generator-assets/admin-base/_skeleton`, client data layer, `services/api/`, auth, backend stamps), Generator's name and place win and host code is moved to match. Only where Generator produces nothing does the host rule choose.
- Admin apps never get thunks or slices from Generator (no `client-redux` output in `apps/admin`); every admin is on admin-base + TanStack Query. Thunk / slice generation is for web and mobile only.
- File names are the same in admin, web and mobile: `services/<feature>.service.ts`, `store/thunks/<feature>.thunk.ts`, `store/slices/<feature>.slice.ts` (Generator output adds `.generated` twins). No camelCase variants (`authSlice.ts`, `*.services.ts`, `*Thunks.ts`); older files are renamed when touched. HTTP infrastructure lives in `services/api/` (`api.generated.ts`, `platform.generated.ts`, `auth.generated.ts`, `common.generated.ts` from Generator; `hooks.ts` project-owned; `frontend.common.mdc`), so the `services/` root holds only `<feature>.service(.generated).ts`.
- Auth comes from Generator (`frontend.common.mdc` "Auth", backend `backend.mdc` "Auth"): G `auth.service/thunk/slice.generated.ts` wrap the once-written K `auth.service.ts` / `auth.thunk.ts` / `auth.slice.ts` where project-specific auth goes. Imports always from `.generated` files; no separate `account.*` layer. Admin keeps auth in Redux (not TanStack).
- Request language is only the `Accept-Language` header (api-contract §1.1, K6): no `lang` / `x-lang` / `?lang=` and no language field in bodies or queries. The default language is per project (Generator assets `en`).
- Scope: Generator is mandatory for `apps/admin` in every host. In user apps (`apps/web`, `apps/mobile`) it is optional: the data layer (service, thunk, slice) may be generated or hand-written. Files that were generated (`.generated` / first line stamp) are still never edited by hand.
- Do not hand-write generated admin config, stamped backend files, or a new entity admin screen (page, table, service, route) in those hosts. Change the model, then generate.
- Run `node /Users/atakanatabey/Projects/AtaAllWorkspace/Generator/scripts/host.mjs admin-config <host> [Entity]` (admin config) or the same command with `generate` (backend), `client <host> <app>` (web / mobile data layer + auth), `client-auth <host> <app>` (auth only). Same functions as the Electron Generate action. `--dry-run` prints paths and writes nothing. Without an entity every module in the manifest is written. The stack is `workspace.backendStack` (detected from the root if missing). Python setup, import and preview: `scripts/python-host.mjs`.
- Before committing a host: `node <Generator>/scripts/drift-check.mjs <host> --generated` must exit 0 (assets and generated files equal Generator output). A difference in a G file is moved to a K file / hook, never kept in the G file. An orphan G file (Generator no longer writes it) is deleted when unused, otherwise its stamp is removed and it becomes project-owned.
- File headers: `// Auto Generated By Generator - <date>` (G and asset-sync files) is Generator's and is overwritten; `// Generated By Generator - <date> (bir kez yazıldı)` (K, skeleton) and files with no header belong to the project. Backend G files start with `<auto-generated by Generator />`.
- Admin UI the config cannot express goes in `packages/admin-base` and is checked with `npm run playground` before a host uses it.
- Still hand-written: `*.generated.ts` (`extendResource`), hooks / custom blocks / `*.Custom.cs`, and non-CRUD pages (login, dashboard, logs, metrics, jobs, screen).

